# steps/named-struct-exec.md §12 (Q45): a `for:` in a named Structure's body is a statement of the body,
# as in a method's body.  Two executions from the root: n counts 3 at each (its declaration runs again),
# the unit's total 6.  Entry 7.
size_t: total 0U
Counter:
    size_t: n 0U
    for: int(i, 0) (i < 3) i++
        n: n + 1U
        total: total + 1U
    end: for
return
Counter
Counter
int: ok 0
if: Counter\n = 3U && total = 6U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
